> isn't there?  He didn't have his mirror along to check.

There are three basic level designs in Hell.  One is the basic labyrinth, with  
nothing special in the middle.  Another is a labyrinth with a small room  
surrounded by a moat in the center.  The Wizard and the Amulet is hiding in one  
of these rooms.  You won't be able to teleport into these rooms, for reasons  
you will discover, but you will be able to dig through the walls.  How you  
cross the moat is up to you.  There are many obvious ways to go, and some not  
so obvious.  The third is Vlad's tower.  On these levels teleporting is  
impossible and some of the walls are un-diggable, as in the castle.  The only  
way in or out of the tower is through the door at the bottom.  These are the  
only levels in Hell that have doors of any kind.

